ding " [:a {:href "/horses/1510"} [:em {} "Lucette"]] ", with six faults, also finishing the course in the fifth fastest time of 2:24.4, although time was only used as a tie-breaker. Finishing second was the defending Olympic champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/12309"} "Tommaso Lequio di Assaba"] " of Italy, who had 8¾ faults in a relatively slow time of 2:42.0. Both riders would return to the Olympics in 1928, but neither would win a medal. Lequio di Assaba also competed in the three-day event in 1924, and would do so again in 1928. He rode " [:a {:href "/horses/2504"} [:em {} "Trebecco"]] " in jumping at all three Olympics, one of the first two horses to appear at three Olympic Games, along with " [:a {:href "/horses/1762"} [:em {} "Nigra"]] ", who also competed from 1920-1928 for American riders.  The bronze medal was won by Poland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/12261"} "Adam Królikiewicz"] ", on " [:a {:href "/horses/1914"} [:em {} "Picador"]] ", in his only Olympic appearance."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "Horse"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Faults"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Jump Faults"] [:th {} "Rider Fall Faults"] [:th {} "Horse Fall Faults"] [:th {} "Obstacle Avoidance Faults"] [:th {} "Time Faults"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12014"} "Alphonse Gemuseus"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/1510"} "Lucette"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SUI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SUI.png"}] "SUI"]] [:td {} "6.00"] [:td {} "2:24.4"] [:td {} "6"] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "0.00"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12309"} "Tommaso Lequio di Assaba"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/2504"} "Trebecco"]]] [:td